From 1eff24249dd14825aba04999d83d5b44ed38a130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:40:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): name every adaptive level cut by rings; read
 only ladder planes

Every arm of machining3d::hsm::plan_level that hands an Adaptive level
to the Offset rings now goes through one helper, rings_named, which
writes "<why> - Offset rings cut <level> instead". The text of each note
is unchanged. If adaptive_passes ever hands back rings without a note
naming the level, plan_level adds one.

The "radius 5.6 cut by rings, no note" seen while working #882 was a
misread by the test reader, not a planner fallback. The 5.0 level's
microlift down ramp put a vertex on 5.6, and the rotary_adaptive reader
took the lifted runs at that height for a level. The reader now reads
only the ladder's own planes (top - k * stepdown).

Pinned by machining3d::hsm::fallback_tests (a developed level the planner
refuses, named by its radius; a planar one, named by its Z; a seam-cut
developed level) and rotary_adaptive's
a_microlift_plane_is_not_read_as_an_unnamed_ring_level.

Fixes #983

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
